WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.542
Pluck woke up one morning earlier than usual.

2
00:00:03.543 --> 00:00:11.464
He could hear his friends outside singing, "Get up! Get up! It's a new day!"

3
00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:15.594
"What should I do today?" he wondered.

4
00:00:15.595 --> 00:00:21.771
"I could pick worms, glide through the air, or clean my feathers.

5
00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:24.695
But none of that sounds like fun."

6
00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:28.189
Pluck was not very excited about the new day.

7
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.784
So Pluck flew off to the riverbank to visit his friend, Duckie.

8
00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:37.274
"Hi Duckie!" Pluck called as he swooped down to the bank.

9
00:00:37.275 --> 00:00:44.011
"Well hello, Pluck. What a nice surprise to see you!" said Duckie.

10
00:00:44.012 --> 00:00:48.094
"Do you have any exciting plans for today?" said Pluck.

11
00:00:48.095 --> 00:00:51.779
"I am bored and don't know what to do."

12
00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.932
"Hmm." Duckie had to think hard.

13
00:00:55.933 --> 00:01:04.406
"You could fly with me up and down the river, or we could dig in the mud to cool off our feet," he offered.

14
00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:06.224
"No, thanks," said Pluck.

15
00:01:06.225 --> 00:01:11.534
"Well, if we have nothing to do at least we can be bored together."

16
00:01:11.535 --> 00:01:15.389
So Pluck and Duckie settled into the bank.

17
00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.289
They watched the flowers opening their faces to the sun.

18
00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:26.038
The flowers bent their stems to get as close to the light as possible. "Ooh!"

19
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:31.007
They watched the fish jump at the bugs, trying to catch some lunch.

20
00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:36.321
The fish jumped high out of the water and made a lot of ripples when they fell back in.

21
00:01:36.322 --> 00:01:43.805
One fish splashed so much that he got Pluck and Duckie wet! "Hey!"

22
00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:51.256
While Pluck and Duckie were trying to shake off the water, they heard a little voice below them start to complain.

23
00:01:51.257 --> 00:01:56.165
"Please stop! You are soaking my home!"

24
00:01:56.166 --> 00:02:02.110
They looked at the ground and saw a row of ants marching food into their hole.

25
00:02:02.111 --> 00:02:06.874
Sure enough, the water from their wings was getting the ground wet.

26
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:12.874
"Oops! We're sorry!" Duckie said, and they moved to the side.

27
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:18.447
"Those ants are really strong!" said Pluck, sounding very impressed.

28
00:02:18.448 --> 00:02:22.884
"Their food is five times bigger than they are!"

29
00:02:22.885 --> 00:02:27.577
After the ants left, Pluck and Duckie looked around.

30
00:02:27.578 --> 00:02:33.458
There was nothing left to see. Duckie lay down and stared at the sky.

31
00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:40.719
"That cloud looks like Big Farmer Parton!" said Duckie, sounding very sure of himself.

32
00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:48.522
"Yeah, I see him! And next to him is Dolly, his little girl!" said Pluck.

33
00:02:48.523 --> 00:02:54.645
As they lay there finding shapes in the clouds, the clouds began to turn pink and purple.

34
00:02:54.646 --> 00:03:02.170
This made the pictures in the sky even more beautiful and helped their imaginations find new shapes in the clouds.

35
00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:07.274
Eventually the pinkish purple colors began to turn to dark blue.

36
00:03:07.275 --> 00:03:12.478
While Pluck and Duckie were watching the clouds, the sun had begun to set.

37
00:03:12.479 --> 00:03:17.891
The flowers began to close their petals. The fish stopped jumping.

38
00:03:17.892 --> 00:03:21.487
The ants shut the door to their hole for the night.

39
00:03:21.488 --> 00:03:25.202
Pluck and Duckie could no longer see the cloud shapes.

40
00:03:25.203 --> 00:03:28.634
Pluck stood up and looked at Duckie.

41
00:03:28.635 --> 00:03:33.722
"Oh no! Duckie, we've wasted the whole day!

42
00:03:33.723 --> 00:03:38.898
We didn't do anything important!" he said disappointedly.

43
00:03:38.899 --> 00:03:44.200
"We didn't waste the day. We did nothing!" said Duckie.

44
00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:48.403
"What?" asked Pluck, sounding confused.

45
00:03:48.404 --> 00:03:52.989
"We don't have to be busy working to have an important day.

46
00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:59.662
Watching everyone else go about their day helped us appreciate the world around us.

47
00:03:59.663 --> 00:04:07.081
I had a wonderful time, but I won't be able to do it again for a little while."

48
00:04:07.082 --> 00:04:09.965
"Why not?" asked Pluck.

49
00:04:09.966 --> 00:04:14.004
He was starting to like the idea of doing nothing every day.

50
00:04:14.005 --> 00:04:19.328
"Because I have work to do tomorrow. Would you like to help?"

51
00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:21.879
"Sure," Pluck agreed.

52
00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:28.035
"Goodnight, Duckie," he said, as he watched him waddle home.

53
00:04:28.036 --> 00:04:34.254
"See you tomorrow for a brand new adventure," Duckie called back.

54
00:04:34.255 --> 00:04:45.729
Pluck flew home for a good night's sleep.

